     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div lang=\"EN-GB\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\" style=\"word-wrap:break-word\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>Will look into SSimp. Thank you Nicola!<u></u><u></u></span></p></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div lang=\"EN-GB\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\" style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<div style=\"border:none;border-top:solid #b5c4df 1.0pt;padding:3.0pt 0cm 0cm 0cm\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:12.0pt\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;color:black\">From:\r\n</span></b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;color:black\">Nicola Pirastu &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">dart...@gmail.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Date: </b>Monday, 11 October 2021 at 21:40<br>\r\n<b>To: </b>Källberg Zvrskovec, Johan &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">johan.kallbe...@kcl.ac.uk</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Cc: </b>Elliot Tucker-Drob &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">tucke...@gmail.com</a>&gt;, Genomic SEM Users &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">genomic-...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;, Breen, Gerome &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">gerome...@kcl.ac.uk</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject: </b>Re: Retaining SNPs in sumstats<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div lang=\"EN-GB\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\" style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><table border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" align=\"left\" width=\"100%\" style=\"width:100.0%;display:table;border-collapse:seperate;float:none\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"background:#a6a6a6;padding:5.25pt 1.5pt 5.25pt 1.5pt\"></td>\r\n<td width=\"100%\" style=\"width:100.0%;background:#eaeaea;padding:5.25pt 3.75pt 5.25pt 11.25pt\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">\r\n<span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif;color:#212121\">You don&#39;t often get email from <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">dart...@gmail.com</a>.\r\n<a href=\"http://aka.ms/LearnAboutSenderIdentification\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://aka.ms/LearnAboutSenderIdentification&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793237639618000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0XAqNwTGFe195fXYQryO0-\">Learn why this is important</a><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"75\" style=\"width:56.25pt;background:#eaeaea;padding:5.25pt 3.75pt 5.25pt 3.75pt\">\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div lang=\"EN-GB\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\" style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:white\">Have you tried SSimp? It allows imputation from summary statistics. Should solve your problem\r\n</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Best<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">N<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:12.0pt\"><a href=\"https://eur03.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fzkutalik%2Fssimp_software&amp;data=04%...%40kcl.ac.uk%7C8b18eedd1e9b430ed8b308d98cf76b37%7C8370cf1416f34c16b83c724071654356%7C0%7C0%7C637695816545169085%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C1000&amp;sdata=HptyvgMJKB0xJGgXrNeGGXo5naDBaIdms%2B2B79X3n5w%3D&amp;reserved=0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://eur03.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url%3Dhttps%253A%252F%252Fgithub.com%252Fzkutalik%252Fssimp_software%26data%3D04%257C01%257Cjohan.kallberg_zvrskovec%2540kcl.ac.uk%257C8b18eedd1e9b430ed8b308d98cf76b37%257C8370cf1416f34c16b83c724071654356%257C0%257C0%257C637695816545169085%257CUnknown%257CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%253D%257C1000%26sdata%3DHptyvgMJKB0xJGgXrNeGGXo5naDBaIdms%252B2B79X3n5w%253D%26reserved%3D0&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793237639618000&amp;usg=AOvVaw305uKYFeGf73-ajqA8qUA9\">https://github.com/zkutalik/ssimp_software</a><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Sent from my iPhone<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br>\r\n<br>\r\n<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<blockquote style=\"margin-top:5.0pt;margin-bottom:5.0pt\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:12.0pt\">On 11 Oct 2021, at 20:34, &#39;Källberg Zvrskovec, Johan&#39; via Genomic SEM Users &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">genomic-...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt; wrote:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</blockquote>\r\n</div>\r\n<blockquote style=\"margin-top:5.0pt;margin-bottom:5.0pt\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">﻿ <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>Thank you for the quick answer on this. I believe I asked a similar question before and got directions to GWAS summary statistics imputation methods. I initially tried using RAISS (﻿<a href=\"https://eur03.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Facademic.oup.com%2Fbioinformatics%2Farticle%2F35%2F22%2F4837%2F5512360&amp;data=04%...%40kcl.ac.uk%7C8b18eedd1e9b430ed8b308d98cf76b37%7C8370cf1416f34c16b83c724071654356%7C0%7C0%7C637695816545179043%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C1000&amp;sdata=pC%2Fs249PIoIG%2BuEsGbCmxbpiyxocHtAB5khoFRZ1HLI%3D&amp;reserved=0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://eur03.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url%3Dhttps%253A%252F%252Facademic.oup.com%252Fbioinformatics%252Farticle%252F35%252F22%252F4837%252F5512360%26data%3D04%257C01%257Cjohan.kallberg_zvrskovec%2540kcl.ac.uk%257C8b18eedd1e9b430ed8b308d98cf76b37%257C8370cf1416f34c16b83c724071654356%257C0%257C0%257C637695816545179043%257CUnknown%257CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%253D%257C1000%26sdata%3DpC%252Fs249PIoIG%252BuEsGbCmxbpiyxocHtAB5khoFRZ1HLI%253D%26reserved%3D0&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793237639618000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1v3mCxeiv_Du0p_yLRKAbe\">https://academic.oup.com/bioinformatics/article/35/22/4837/5512360</a>)\r\n but abandoned it as most datasets had good coverage, but not all unfortunately. A summary data level imputation step would definitely help when running userGWAS.</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span> </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<div style=\"border:none;border-top:solid #b5c4df 1.0pt;padding:3.0pt 0cm 0cm 0cm\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:12.0pt\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;color:black\">From:\r\n</span></b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;color:black\">Elliot Tucker-Drob &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">tucke...@gmail.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Date: </b>Monday, 11 October 2021 at 17:23<br>\r\n<b>To: </b>Källberg Zvrskovec, Johan &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">johan.kallbe...@kcl.ac.uk</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Cc: </b>Genomic SEM Users &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">genomic-...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject: </b>Re: Retaining SNPs in sumstats</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<table border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" align=\"left\" width=\"100%\" style=\"width:100.0%;display:table;border-collapse:seperate;float:none\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"background:#a6a6a6;padding:5.25pt 1.5pt 5.25pt 1.5pt\"></td>\r\n<td width=\"100%\" style=\"width:100.0%;background:#eaeaea;padding:5.25pt 3.75pt 5.25pt 11.25pt\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">\r\n<span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif;color:#212121\">You don&#39;t often get email from <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">tucke...@gmail.com</a>.\r\n<a href=\"http://aka.ms/LearnAboutSenderIdentification\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://aka.ms/LearnAboutSenderIdentification&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793237639618000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0XAqNwTGFe195fXYQryO0-\">Learn why this is important</a></span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"75\" style=\"width:56.25pt;background:#eaeaea;padding:5.25pt 3.75pt 5.25pt 3.75pt\">\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:white\">You would need to impute each sample to the same reference panel and redo the\r\n</span>Univariate GWASs… <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Otherwise you are in the same territory that is common for cross-referencing hits across GWASs where you might do something like find a proxy SNP for a variant of interest that isn’t genotypes or imputed..  <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I can think of more creative solutions off the top of my head but we haven’t tested or implemented those. <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">On Mon, Oct 11, 2021 at 10:32 AM &#39;Johan Zvrskovec&#39; via Genomic SEM Users &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">genomic-...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt; wrote:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border:none;border-left:solid #cccccc 1.0pt;padding:0cm 0cm 0cm 6.0pt;margin-left:4.8pt;margin-top:5.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:5.0pt\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Hi, <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Do you have suggestions for maximising the number of SNP&#39;s retained by the sumstats() function? It seems to only keep the intersect of variants across all indicator variable datasets. Is there an easy way to impute missing values, maybe\r\n using the previously fitted latent factor structure?<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Kind regards<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Johan<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;Genomic SEM Users&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to\r\n<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">genomic-sem-us...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo view this discussion on the web visit <a href=\"https://eur03.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fgroups.google.com%2Fd%2Fmsgid%2Fgenomic-sem-users%2F6c540fef-dc57-441e-ab1d-5ff2818ebaaan%2540googlegroups.com%3Futm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter&amp;data=04%...%40kcl.ac.uk%7C8b18eedd1e9b430ed8b308d98cf76b37%7C8370cf1416f34c16b83c724071654356%7C0%7C0%7C637695816545179043%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C1000&amp;sdata=1Oc%2FsvK51%2FQtcJ5UUGtYOBGYbbwdvAIEJz%2FoUq7L2O4%3D&amp;reserved=0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://eur03.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url%3Dhttps%253A%252F%252Fgroups.google.com%252Fd%252Fmsgid%252Fgenomic-sem-users%252F6c540fef-dc57-441e-ab1d-5ff2818ebaaan%252540googlegroups.com%253Futm_medium%253Demail%2526utm_source%253Dfooter%26data%3D04%257C01%257Cjohan.kallberg_zvrskovec%2540kcl.ac.uk%257C8b18eedd1e9b430ed8b308d98cf76b37%257C8370cf1416f34c16b83c724071654356%257C0%257C0%257C637695816545179043%257CUnknown%257CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%253D%257C1000%26sdata%3D1Oc%252FsvK51%252FQtcJ5UUGtYOBGYbbwdvAIEJz%252FoUq7L2O4%253D%26reserved%3D0&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793237639618000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3E6GoC8NA7zK9nSdo7rpGH\">\r\nhttps://groups.google.com/d/msgid/genomic-sem-users/6c540fef-dc57-441e-ab1d-5ff2818ebaaan%40googlegroups.com</a>.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</blockquote>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;Genomic SEM Users&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to\r\n<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">genomic-sem-us...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo view this discussion on the web visit <a href=\"https://eur03.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fgroups.google.com%2Fd%2Fmsgid%2Fgenomic-sem-users%2FAM7PR03MB649997A7BBFE491D6CAF3586F0B59%2540AM7PR03MB6499.eurprd03.prod.outlook.com%3Futm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter&amp;data=04%...%40kcl.ac.uk%7C8b18eedd1e9b430ed8b308d98cf76b37%7C8370cf1416f34c16b83c724071654356%7C0%7C0%7C637695816545188998%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C1000&amp;sdata=cZZcYJmr9SWdBmw4Lh%2FmfG4FJjjwYeHFADDIM4dMA1A%3D&amp;reserved=0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://eur03.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url%3Dhttps%253A%252F%252Fgroups.google.com%252Fd%252Fmsgid%252Fgenomic-sem-users%252FAM7PR03MB649997A7BBFE491D6CAF3586F0B59%252540AM7PR03MB6499.eurprd03.prod.outlook.com%253Futm_medium%253Demail%2526utm_source%253Dfooter%26data%3D04%257C01%257Cjohan.kallberg_zvrskovec%2540kcl.ac.uk%257C8b18eedd1e9b430ed8b308d98cf76b37%257C8370cf1416f34c16b83c724071654356%257C0%257C0%257C637695816545188998%257CUnknown%257CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%253D%257C1000%26sdata%3DcZZcYJmr9SWdBmw4Lh%252FmfG4FJjjwYeHFADDIM4dMA1A%253D%26reserved%3D0&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793237639618000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3YXIjY1RuFK6uuJGOZnWbW\">\r\nhttps://groups.google.com/d/msgid/genomic-sem-users/AM7PR03MB649997A7BBFE491D6CAF3586F0B59%40AM7PR03MB6499.eurprd03.prod.outlook.com</a>.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</blockquote>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div></div>"
    ]
